course: dictionary
lesson: 8526
title: Savage: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on who uses them and where. Savage is a good example. Its main meaning is very fierce and cruel, as in «a savage attack by a wild animal». Read the words around it to find the right meaning.
explain: In Alice's story, the White Rabbit worries the Duchess will be «savage» if kept waiting. The clue is the waiting: nobody likes to be kept waiting, so savage here means furious. Test it: "the Duchess will be furious if kept waiting" still makes sense.
explain: Slang changes things again. If a friend says, «That comeback was savage!», they mean it was bold, sharp and funny, not that anyone was attacked. Savage can also mean very harsh, as in «savage cuts to spending».
explain: Be careful with one old meaning. Long ago, some Europeans used «savages» to describe other peoples. This was unfair and racist, so we do not use the word that way about people today. You will learn more about it in history lessons.
fact: Savage means very fierce, violent and cruel, like a savage attack.
fact: «Savage» can mean furious, as in the Duchess who will be «savage» if kept waiting in Alice's story.
fact: «Savage» can mean very harsh, as in «savage criticism».
fact: To savage something is to attack it fiercely, with teeth or with words; to be «savaged by a dog» means to be badly bitten.
fact: Calling people «savages» was offensive and unfair, so never use it about people today.
exercise: «The White Rabbit worries the Duchess will be savage if kept waiting.» What does savage mean here? | Wild and hairy | *Furious | Sleepy | Hungry
exercise: «A savage storm tore the roof off the barn.» What does savage describe? | Slightly warm | *Very fierce and violent | Very quiet and calm | Very small
exercise: Your friend says, «That comeback was savage!» What does it probably mean? | *It was bold, sharp and funny | It was very quiet | It was a long story | Someone was hurt by a wild animal
test: A dog can savage a sheep. What does savage mean here? | To wash it gently | *To attack it fiercely | To count it | To feed it slowly
test: Why do we not call people «savages» today? | Because it means very happy | *Because it was unfair and racist about other peoples | Because it is too short | Because it is a fancy word
exam: Read this: «Savage cuts to spending hurt the school.» What does savage mean? | Very small and soft | Very happy | Very kind and generous | *Very harsh and severe
